czi2tif: convert a Zeiss CZI mosaic to a compact tiled JPEG BigTIFF.

The container streams the CZI one tile-row at a time (bounded memory) and
writes a tiled, JPEG-compressed (Q90) BigTIFF with a 1/1.8 gamma applied.
This TIFF is a small, fast-to-produce intermediate meant to feed a downstream
pyramid/retiling pipeline (e.g. libvips); it is not the final deliverable.

Reader: upstream `czifile` package (cloned from GitHub during Docker build).

Build:
    docker build --platform linux/amd64 -t czi .

Build with czifile pinned to a specific release tag:
    docker build --platform linux/amd64 -t czi \
    --build-arg CZIFILE_REF=v2026.6.12 .

Optional build args:
    CZIFILE_REPO (default: https://github.com/cgohlke/czifile.git)
    CZIFILE_REF  (release tag, branch, or commit; default: v2026.6.12)

Run (paths are relative to the mounted working directory):
    docker run -it --platform linux/amd64 -v `pwd`:/root/ czi input.czi output.tif

If the output path is omitted, `input.czi.tif` is written next to the input.

Run without Docker:
    pip install -r requirements.txt
    pip install "git+https://github.com/cgohlke/czifile.git@v2026.6.12"
    python3 czi2tif.py input.czi output.tif